Rehabilitation construction starts for Dharavi.

@PranavAdani, Director, Adani Enterprises Limited (AEL), performed the Bhoomi Poojan at the 22-acre Matunga railway site.

Aseem Kumar Gupta, Additional Chief Secretary, Urban Development Department, Government of Maharashtra, was the Guest of Honour. Dr Mahendra Kalyankar, CEO, Dharavi Redevelopment Project/Slum Rehabilitation Authority (DRP/SRA), also attended the event.

The project envisages safe, modern homes for families, along with the infrastructure and amenities needed for a better quality of life. The rehabilitation buildings at Matunga will have a kindergarten, community hall, podium gardens and sit-out areas.

Ten per cent of the commercial space in each rehabilitation building will be reserved to generate revenue for common infrastructure upkeep. Adani Navbharat Developers Private Limited (ANDPL) will maintain the buildings and shared infrastructure for the first 10 years after handover.

